## ANANTA at a glance

ANANTA is a free-to-play urban open-world RPG from Naked Rain Studio, published by NetEase Games. NetEase announced at Gamescom 2026 that it **launches worldwide on 15 January 2027**. The official website carries the same date, checked 27 November 2026.

The US Steam listing currently shows **14 January 2027**. Global launches often start on the evening of the day before in the Americas, but NetEase hasn't published a launch time yet, so check your region's store page closer to the date.

## What we know so far

- **Developer:** Naked Rain Studio. **Publisher:** NetEase Games.
- **Release date:** 15 January 2027, worldwide.
- **Price:** free to play. Steam lists it under Free To Play.
- **Platforms:** ANANTA's own PC client, PC (Steam), PlayStation 5 and mobile, according to NetEase's launch-date announcement.
- **Pre-registrations:** over 17 million across 110 countries and regions, according to the same announcement.
- **Trailers:** the official site shows a Launch Date Trailer, a Gameplay Trailer and a Gameplay Video.

## Go viral, save the world

NetEase sums up the premise as "Go Viral. Save the World." You play a newcomer to Nova City who builds a reputation as an influencer. Missions, crises and side adventures all grow your social influence, which opens up new resources and perks. In the gameplay video, you arrive as the new captain of a special task force whose company collapses almost as soon as you report for duty.

You recruit a team of agents to rebuild that task force, and you can switch between playable characters. The Steam page mentions roles such as a police officer, a hacker and a gang leader.

## Two cities

- **Nova City:** the main modern city, with business districts, back alleys, quiet tea towns and busy old streets, according to the Steam description.
- **Chongxiao:** a second major city inspired by modern China. NetEase revealed it in the launch-date trailer, and the store page says you can fly back there to find secrets in a place your character thought they knew well.

## Getting around and fighting

According to the Steam description, you can drive cars, ride bikes, sail and fly, and swing between buildings. NetEase says anywhere you can see, you can go. Combat is martial-arts based and plays out in the streets. The city runs on a 24-hour cycle, with events such as late-night street races.

## PC requirements

Steam lists Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit) and "TBD" for the processor and graphics card, so the real PC requirements aren't published yet. The official site notes that ANANTA is adding NVIDIA DLSS 4.5.

## What's still unconfirmed

- **Launch time:** no exact hour has been announced, which is why the Steam date shows 14 January in the US.
- **Monetisation details:** the game is free to play, but the pages we checked don't explain how character recruitment or purchases work.
- **Cross-play and shared progress:** not stated on the pages we checked.
- **Performance:** we haven't played ANANTA.

## Official sources

- [ANANTA on Steam](https://store.steampowered.com/app/4814120/?l=english): free-to-play listing, US release date, description and requirements, checked 27 November 2026.
- [Official ANANTA site](https://www.anantagame.com/): global release date and trailers, checked 27 November 2026.
- [NetEase launch-date announcement on Games Press](https://www.gamespress.com/ANANTA-the-Highly-Anticipated-Urban-Open-World-RPG-Announces-January-1): platforms, premise, Chongxiao and pre-registrations, published 25 August 2026.

This is a researched pre-release article, not a review or a hands-on preview.
